"view.prenatal.col.type"                = "Type";
"view.prenatal.col.prenataldate"        = "Prenatal date/time";
"view.prenatal.results.help"            = "You get a table with, in the first column, the date on which a position takes effect. Next you see the prenatally formed aspect, eclipse, ingress, or change between direct and retrograde. The following columns show the positions of the prenatal factor and those of the radix factor. In the last column you see the prenatal moment.\n\nTo correct the prenatal moment, select an event in the left panel by clicking on it. You can add events using the 'New Event' button, or you can directly enter a date and time. You link the entered date and time to a prenatal moment by clicking on it. A 'Combine' button then appears, and clicking it links the prenatal moment to the event. This results in an adjusted conception date. The standard conception date (without correction) and the actual conception date (with correction) are shown in the left panel. Clicking 'Reset' returns you to the initial situation.";

